--
pointer handling for concurrency is unsound
^warning: ignoring
--
Tests that may-alias correctly handles type-compatible (same bit-width)
types. shared_ptr is int* but points to unsigned int. Without the type
compatibility relaxation, the may-alias object would not alias with
val_unsigned and the assertion would incorrectly fail.
